<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luxeuil Abbey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 590</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Abbey of Luxeuil</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luxeuil Abbey was a monastery founded by the Irish missionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/columbanus">Columbanus</a> around 590 at Luxeuil, in the foothills of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vosges">Vosges</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>. It became one of the most influential monasteries of Merovingian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, training monks who founded many further houses under Columbanus's strict rule. Columbanus was expelled around 610 after quarrelling with King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theuderic-ii">Theuderic II</a> and his grandmother Brunhild, but the abbey flourished for centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luxeuil-abbey.jpg" alt="Luxeuil Abbey" width="320" height="292" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: A.BourgeoisP · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2020-08_-_Monast%C3%A8re_de_Luxeuil_-_06.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
